# ZP = { (2i,j) | (i,j) \in Z^2, 1 <= i,j <= 100 }
#   (i is even, and j is between i and i+100)
# 
# T = (i,j) -> (2i+10, 3i+j+1)
# T is not unimodular, but spreads the same lattice as the Z-polyhedron
# so this preimage is in Z^d and keeps the same number of points.
